This is a fun, albeit relatively short game.
The good:
- Loved the upbeat music and its variations;
- Visually nice to look at;
- Not too hard, though Legendary mode is enraging but satisfying at the same time;
- Honestly, it looks super pretty;
- Mouse controls are tight;
- Replay value;
- The price is right.
The bad:
- Too short? Though for this price I wouldn't expect the game to be any longer;
- As a Linux user, there was a little issue with the achievements at first, thanks to which I will never unlock the 'legendary weapon' achievement, which is kind of a bummer;
EDIT 01/11: I managed to unlock the achievement after all after some more fiddling around so this only serves as a warning relevant to Linux users. Check the discussions for a step-by-step on how to get the achievements working :).
- No controller support, though I wouldn't recommend that anyway for this game.
(edit: spelling and another good thing added)
TL;DR: I had a hard time coming up with anything bad at all. I really like this game.

